        ]
      },
      "worked": "Since $4\\equiv-1\\pmod5$, $3\\equiv-2\\pmod5$ and $5\\equiv0\\pmod5$, and 99 is odd,\n$$\\begin{align*}1^{99}+2^{99}+3^{99}+4^{99}+5^{99}&\\equiv1^{99}+2^{99}+(-2)^{99}+(-1)^{99}+0\\pmod5\\\\1^{99}+2^{99}+3^{99}+4^{99}+5^{99}&\\equiv1+2^{99}-2^{99}-1\\pmod5\\\\1^{99}+2^{99}+3^{99}+4^{99}+5^{99}&\\equiv0\\pmod5.\\end{align*}$$\nThe remainder is $0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
